# Development workflow (ACSO)

## Hosting strategy

- **Legacy prod** (`samoorg.com.ua`, account `samoorg`, shared «Потужний»): **PHP 7.3**, WP ~5.3 — **do not change PHP** on this account; **read-only** for automation until cutover.
- **New stack**: separate **cheap hosting account** (e.g. Hostpro Cloud Site) with **PHP 8.2/8.3**, clean WP, own DB and SSH — **all theme/plugin dev and staging writes** there.
- **One PHP per cPanel account** on classic shared — no MultiPHP on current plan (`multiphp` unavailable). Different PHP versions = **different accounts**, not subdomain tricks.
- Optional later: **Multiadmin / Reseller** if many sites under one billing — not required for two environments.

## Git — source of truth (local repo)

**Commit:**

- `wp-content/themes/acso-child/` (when it exists in repo)
- `prototype/`
- `_docs/`, `scripts/`, `.cursor/rules/`, `.agents/rules/`

**Do not commit:** `secrets/acso.env`, `wp-config.php`, WP core, `uploads/`, server vendor, `_backups/`.

**Do not** use server as primary Git for application code; deploy **from repo → staging**, not edit-only-on-server.

## What we deploy to the server (SSH only, staging / new account)

| Artifact | Target | Tool |
|----------|--------|------|
| Static **prototype** | `…/ui/` on staging docroot (never prod) | `scripts/deploy-staging-ui.sh` (tar/rsync over SSH) |
| **acso-child** theme | `wp-content/themes/acso-child/` on **new/staging** WP | SSH rsync/tar when theme exists |
| WP core, plugins, DB | Installed on server (WP admin / Toolkit / host); **not** in Git |

**FTP** — human fallback only; **prefer SSH** for agent and scripts.

## Local machine

- **No full local WordPress** (no Docker WP sandbox required).
- **UX / layout:** `prototype/` static HTML → deploy to `/ui/` for approval.
- **Real WP behavior:** test on **remote staging** URL; screenshots/Playwright against staging, not mandatory local WP.

## WordPress tooling (no host MCP)

- **cPanel MCP:** disabled on shared (`apitokens` off) — use **SSH + `uapi`** and cPanel UI.
- **WP admin:** humans for Elementor, menus, plugins; **prod admin not for agent writes**.
- **Agent automation on staging:** **REST API** + **Application Password** (`STAGING_WP_*` in `secrets/acso.env`); optional local MCP wrapping REST — **not** host “AI agents”.
- **WP-CLI:** use `wp` when present (cPanel WP Toolkit on skm352); else `wp-cli.phar` in `~/bin`. Not bundled with WP wizard — check `which wp`.

## Databases

- **One MySQL database per WordPress instance** — never share one DB between old and new site.
- Prod DB names stay on prod account; new site = **new empty DB** on new account.

## Cutover (blue-green)

1. Build **complete site** on **new account** (PHP 8.x, theme, content migration, 301 table prepared).
2. Test on **temporary URL** / second domain until sign-off.
3. Before switch: lower **DNS TTL**, **final content sync** if needed, **backup prod** (files + DB).
4. **Cutover:** point **DNS** `samoorg.com.ua` to **new hosting IP**; SSL; smoke test; enable **301** (Redirection).
5. **Old account:** keep **rollback** window (weeks) — do not delete immediately; may become **preprod/archive**, not twin prod.
6. **Do not** mutate legacy prod for experiments after cutover except agreed rollback.

## Env files

- `secrets/acso.env` — SSH, staging/new-host URLs, DB, `STAGING_WP_*`, cPanel; **never log or commit**.
- When second account exists: add clearly named vars (e.g. `NEW_HOST_*` or second `STAGING_*` block) — keep **prod vs new** unambiguous for every command.

## Backups

- Full file backup **before cutover** or risky prod work — not required **only** for PHP version reasoning on legacy (PHP does not delete files); **do** backup before DNS switch and before ETL loads.
- Mac: `_backups/` in project (gitignored); rsync needs **rsync 3.x** + `--iconv` for legacy Cyrillic upload names on Apple rsync 2.6.
